Jove <invalid@invalid.invalid> wrote:
>  In this light, over preparing so you get a free ride down to 
>the Vibrating Square just means *even more* frustration with the 
>"mysterious force" throwing you back down levels in Gehennom
>when ascending with the Amulet of Yendor.

Preparing for the section of the game between the Castle and Rodney is
pretty trivial.  Frankly, if you can clear the main dungeon including
the Castle, Gehennom holds few terrors, and the two worst of those
(Rodney and Demogorgon) can be oneshotted with only a modest amount of
preparation, while purple 'L' can be wiped with a single blessed scroll
of genocide.

I'm *much* less of an overpreparer than DJSD, and I still have
essentially no trouble with the stretch of the game between clearing
the Castle and confronting Rodney.  The point of overpreparation is not
to survive that stretch of the game - that's mostly trivial if you aren't
playing genoless, which is why that stage of the game is so deadly boring
(oh, and leaving purple 'L' in play doesn't make it interesting, it
makes it irritating).  The point of overpreparation is to survive the
trip *out* of the dungeon and through the elemental planes.

Some number soup, while I'm here.

The average number of levels by which one rises when going up stairs in
Gehennom with a lawful character carrying the amulet is 
(0.75 * 1 + 0.0625 * 0 - 0.0625 * 1 - 0.0625 * 2 - 0.0625 * 3) = 0.375.

A neutral character averages 0.5 levels per ascent and a chaotic character
averages 0.625 levels per ascent.  Furthermore, the outliers for chaotic
and neutral characters are less harsh.

